## Summary

For vLLM #49980, initialization-time sizing is correct and graph-stable but reserves request metadata for max_num_seqs multiplied by maximum local-attention chunk expansion. The guarded grow-on-demand design is preferable: allocate only on overflow, size to observed virtual requests/pages, and refuse pointer replacement after any CUDA-graph decode wrapper exists. ChunkedLocalAttention advertises AttentionCGSupport.NEVER, so the affected long-prefill path can grow without invalidating captured addresses. Preserve a CPU regression for the virtual-batch expansion trigger and require GPU serving plus graph-mode validation before upstreaming.

## Outcome

Initialization-capacity candidate rejected; guarded grow-on-demand selected for publication.

